-- title:
--   Cokernel of Frobenius counts the Dieudonné module of B
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, and let $A$ be a commutative ring carrying a Hopf algebra structure over $\mathbb{Z}/p$ whose comultiplication is cocommutative and which is finite as a $\mathbb{Z}/p$-module; assume the Cartier dual of $A$, that is the dual module $\operatorname{Hom}_{\mathbb{Z}/p}(A,\mathbb{Z}/p)$ with its convolution ring structure, is a local ring. Let $F_k \colon A \to A$ be a $\mathbb{Z}/p$-bialgebra homomorphism with $F_k(x) = x^{p}$ for all $x$. Let $B$ be a commutative ring with a $\mathbb{Z}/p$-bialgebra structure and $q \colon A \to B$ a surjective bialgebra homomorphism whose kernel, as an ideal of $A$, is the ideal generated by the image under $F_k$ of the augmentation ideal $\ker(\varepsilon_A)$. Write $M(C)$ for the Dieudonné module of a $\mathbb{Z}/p$-bialgebra $C$, namely the direct limit, along the shift maps, of the additive subgroups of $\mathrm{W}_n(C)$ consisting of those truncated Witt vectors $x$ with $\mathrm{W}_n(\Delta)(x) = \mathrm{W}_n(\iota_1)(x) + \mathrm{W}_n(\iota_2)(x)$, where $\Delta$ is the comultiplication and $\iota_1,\iota_2 \colon C \to C \otimes C$ are the two inclusions. Then the quotient of $M(A)$ by the range of the Frobenius endomorphism (induced levelwise by the Witt-vector Frobenius) and $M(B)$ have the same cardinality, as an equality of values of `Nat.card`.
--
--   For a finite commutative unipotent group scheme $G = \operatorname{Spec} A$ over $\mathbb{F}_p$ with Frobenius kernel $G[F] = \operatorname{Spec} B$, this is the count $\#\bigl(M(G)/F\,M(G)\bigr) = \#M(G[F])$ for the contravariant Dieudonné module. It supplies the Frobenius side of the rank-symmetry statement [`Deformation.DieudonneModule.natCard_ker_frobenius_eq_natCard_quot_range_verschiebung_of_nonempty_bialgEquiv_cartierDual_zmodp`](thm.html#Deformation.DieudonneModule.natCard_ker_frobenius_eq_natCard_quot_range_verschiebung_of_nonempty_bialgEquiv_cartierDual_zmodp).
